  "headline": "Sertraline hydrochloride is not on FDA's shortage list as of 2026-10-21; supply traces to a registered repack plant last classified VAI on 2025-05-27",
  "headline_cites": ["D4", "E9", "E8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list does not include sertraline hydrochloride as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale East, Corvale General, and Corvale Lakeside carries NDC 68788404503 and labeler Preferred Pharmaceuticals Inc.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The label identifies Preferred Pharmaceuticals Inc. as a registered repack plant (FEI 3004582966).",
      "cites": ["E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA's most recent inspection of that plant ended 2025-05-27 and was classified VAI, with the classification known on 2025-07-30.",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale Lakeside holds 15 tablets at 1.8 per day, giving 8.5 days on hand, below a two‑week buffer.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 208 tablets at 6.7 per day, giving 31.1 days on hand and can spare 10 tablets while retaining at least two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The recommended action is to transfer 10 tablets of 25 mg from Corvale East to Corvale Lakeside, which would bring Lakeside to roughly 14 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    }
  ]
}
